## Critical Notes
<critical>
- ALWAYS validate type variants before any ownership transfer
- ALWAYS mark struct bindings as mutable when using std::mem::take
- NEVER move fields directly unless struct can be partially moved
- Ensure field types implement Default or provide default value
- Document ownership transfer for complex scenarios
- Consider cloning instead if performance impact is acceptable
- When extracting multiple values:
  1. Validate types and structure first
  2. Handle references/copies second
  3. Move owned values last
  4. Keep operations separate and clear
  5. Document the sequence of operations
- For RISC0 receipts:
  1. Validate and convert receipt type first
  2. Handle dev mode receipts appropriately
  3. Validate journal structure before ownership transfer
  4. Extract digests before taking journal ownership
  5. Use std::mem::take for journal extraction
  6. Maintain receipt validity throughout
  7. Document ownership transfer sequence
  8. Emit appropriate metrics for failures
- For MaybePruned types:
  1. Use pattern matching for each nested level
  2. Check for pruned data before accessing values
  3. Handle all error cases with proper context
  4. Extract references before moving data
  5. Follow receipt claim hierarchy
  6. Emit metrics for pruned data
  7. Use proper error types for each failure case
  8. Document MaybePruned handling strategy
- For complex ownership scenarios:
  1. Order operations from least to most invasive
  2. Use references for validation and inspection
  3. Take ownership only after all preconditions are met
  4. Keep struct valid for remaining operations
  5. Document ownership transfer sequence
  6. Handle error cases with appropriate metrics
</critical> 